{
  "_about": "Engine manifest: one entry per registered engine command (status planned, no code yet), per gate the engine runs (status on, card MW-003, with on_failure_reason: one line per gate) and per written but unregistered gate (status off-today). A gate in two groups has two entries on one function (MW-003 decision 1). Replaced by MW-003: rule_lock, card_test_lock, rule_code_lock, process_lock and discussion_freeze by lock, subtask_gate by subtask; the lock_notice entries are deleted, lock_notice joins the start line (D-1). Product checks are not here; they come from the branch profile's product_checks[]. name is unique; gate is the profile switch (gates.<gate>.on). group is the dispatcher group: one hook entry per event and group, `mkway/engine/mkway.py hook <event> --group <group>` (decision C10: start, edit, shell, post, prompt, stop). function is the gate's module:function, null until the gate is written (card MW-003); reason_ids lists the reason ids the gate may return, and a gate with none is not loaded. matcher null = no matcher (every tool); the dispatcher filters each gate by its own matcher. An entry's onFailure is applied by the dispatcher per gate (block = refuse gate-error; anything else = allow); 'none' is the source's word for no blocking. groups is the group table, an engine constant (R13c): the hook entry of a group carries the group's onFailure (edit and shell: block, so a timeout or crash of the dispatcher blocks the tool call); turning a gate on never changes it. class (MW-012) is integrity or form; a missing class reads integrity. An integrity gate never degrades and never reads a watch marker; a form gate may go into watch mode (see engine/gatemode.py).",
